      "text": "Let's denote the two numbers as \\( x \\) and \\( y \\). According to the problem, we have two equations:\n\n1. \\( x + y = 6 \\)\n2. \\( x^2 - y^2 = 12 \\)\n\nWe can use the difference of squares formula to rewrite the second equation:\n\\[\nx^2 - y^2 = (x+y)(x-y)\n\\]\n\nSubstituting \\( x + y = 6 \\) into the formula, we get:\n\\[\n6(x - y) = 12\n\\]\n\nSolving for \\( x - y \\), we divide both sides by 6:\n\\[\nx - y = \\frac{12}{6} = 2\n\\]\n\nThus, the positive difference between the two numbers is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{2}\n\\]",
